# Project structure

```
index.html              HTML template: meta tags, JSON-LD, the inline script that restores theme and contrast
rspack.config.ts        two builds: the client bundle and the prerender bundle
scripts/prerender.ts    renders the page into dist/index.html
scripts/fetch-stats.ts  refreshes src/data/stats.json from GitHub and npm
public/                 files copied to dist as they are
src/
  App.tsx               composes the sections in page order
  index.tsx             client entry, hydrates
  entry-server.tsx      prerender entry
  index.css             @import list only
  components/           one component per section, plus Hud, Palette, Xray
  constants/            copy and static data
  styles/               one stylesheet per section
  types/interfaces.ts   shared types
  utils/                signals, formatting and the imperative code
  data/stats.json       generated, never edited by hand
```

## Placement
- Copy and static data go in `src/constants`. Components import them.
- Pure functions go in `src/utils`. Shared signals and mutable session state live in `src/utils/session.ts`.
- Types shared by more than one file go in `src/types/interfaces.ts`.
- A constant or helper used by one component only, and a few lines long, stays in that component.
- Keep components under 200 lines. Move data and pure helpers out before splitting the JSX.
- Imperative code that owns a canvas or a foreign runtime stays out of components: `glyphs.ts` (WebGL2 code rain), `reactDemo.ts` (the React 18 island), `loop.ts` and `engine.ts` (the frame loop and its wiring), `cv.ts` (the PDF).
